  Before approaches, one thing I need to resolve, because it inverts the change you originally asked for. Right now
  [38;5;153mlogin()[39m is a stub ([38;5;153mapp.js:4-8[39m) that fabricates [38;5;153m{ success: true, user: username }[39m and never actually calls
  [38;5;153mAPI_ENDPOINT[39m. A [3mreal[0m user identifier generally can't be passed [1minto[0m login — pre-authentication, the app only knows
  what someone typed into a form, and a client-chosen "user ID" is self-asserted, not real. The usual shape is the
  reverse: login authenticates, the server [1mreturns[0m the canonical userId, the app persists it, and everything downstream
  reads it from there. That's [38;5;153mlogin()[39m returning a userId, not accepting one.

